{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-evidence` skill MUST be the home of the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message for a change to agreed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires `habeas-evidence` to be the home of seven topics: the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message. All of them are covered by the one marked test, `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_is_home_of_authoring_findings_and_assessment_outcomes]`.\n\nPresence in the home skill, one assertion per topic:\n- **Authoring workflow:** the `## Workflow` section of `SKILL.md` must contain `` `habeas author --all` ``.\n- **Fixing findings:** `## Fixing findings` must contain the `| Finding | Action |` table header and the `### Missing test and example references` subsection.\n- **Disagreeing assessments:** `## Disagreeing assessments` must contain `The goal is`.\n- **Commit message:** `## Rules` must contain `in the message of the commit that makes it`.\n- **FIXME judgments:** `references/fixme.md` must contain `# FIXME judgments`.\n- **Citation and site reviews:** `references/reviews.md` must contain both `## Citation reviews` and `## Site reviews`.\n- **Outcomes:** no section-specific assertion, but `assert_home` covers it through the marker `A judgment is one of three outcomes` in `home_markers`.\n\nExactly one home:\n- `assert_home(\"habeas-evidence\")` runs `assert_phrases` against the whole skill (`SKILL.md` plus `references/`), so every `home_markers` entry for this skill must be present.\n- Those markers include the outcomes, authoring-workflow, fixing-findings, FIXME, citation-review, site-review, disagreeing-assessments and commit-message statements.\n- It then asserts that none of the other four skills (`SKILLS`) contains any of those markers. A topic stated in full in a second skill would therefore fail.\n- `skill_files` lists each skill's `SKILL.md` and `references/` files, which matches the definition of a skill in `requirements.cli.skill_structure`.\n\nI found no gap. A skill that restated a topic in different words would pass the exclusivity check, but the text gives no finer criterion for \"stated in full\". The marker approach is a reasonable reading of it. The `section` helper strips code fences when finding heading boundaries, and `assert_text` checks `contains` with a labelled failure message, so the assertions do enforce the expected outcome.",
  "references": "705ed82e4b6db789bc1e43ba36e10077d3f5b824870ae00641b8c90ee5333b95",
